ues  okay  that is the bottom line what is who  benefits who doesn't benefit  remain focused on the economics that's  um i think always going to work much  better and actually deliver for people  not just focus on economic policies that  will create more redistribution  redistribution of wealth but really  deliver i think the vaccine  is a sign that there can be like  publicly funded health initiatives yeah  and that  you should focus on that you should hope  we should focus on creating  um strong infrastructure within public  health universal health care  universal quality child care all of  these bread and butter issues that  people need in their lives desperately  right  now and if you can produce that then you  can produce a sense of the collective  you can produce a sense of progressive  liberal policies that work for people  yes and so in that sense  they should not take the bait the left  should not take debate on the cultural  issues they should absolutely deflect  and i and you know i've had my i've been  agnostic on biden but i do feel like  he's much more progressive than obama  and that his um stimulus packages be  something that is  executed with the greatest fervor and  authority and here's  here's one thing i'm going to um um end  with is that  i'm not playing the pm the pmc blame  game where i say oh  the pmc they're all bad no we need good  professionals  we can't have infrastructural  reconstruction of this country  without return to the professional  standards  of both like stock broking or you know  researching universities or um policy  making and think tanks  that is shielded from the market right  now all of these knowledge workers are  so  driven by profit and we need to go back  to  non-market professional standards of  being  and that's i think something that we  often lose track of in the left and  we think like oh um anybody who's a  bureaucrat is bad  how are you going to spend 1.9 trillion  dollars  correctly or well without a good  functioning bureaucracy without a good  functioning government  that's why i have no patience for the  anarcho  leftists yes you and me both you and me  both uh the book is virtue hoarders  the case against the professional  managerial class we've been speaking  of course with the book's author  professor catherine liu so great to have  you on today  thank you david thank you so much
 

